# Build context: the five sources the Dockerfile copies, and nothing else.
#
# The context names the products rather than the folders that are not products, so a checkout that
# grows another top-level directory needs no amendment here and no directory joins the context for
# being unnamed. A deny list has the opposite property: `.worktrees/` holds a feature worktree per
# branch, and a pattern written for the root (`node_modules/`, `.git/`) does not match a nested one,
# so the daemon receives gigabytes it never reads.
#
# Everything the image needs is copied by name in the Dockerfile — keep the two lists together.
*

!package.json
!package-lock.json
!tsconfig.json
!src
!schemas
